  眉开眼笑 | méi kāi yǎn xiào | brows open and eyes smile; beaming with delight
  面无表情 | miàn wú biǎo qíng | poker-faced; showing zero facial emotion
  情不自禁 | qíng bù zì jìn | cannot help doing something; overcome by emotion

character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  表 | biǎo | surface; outside; manifest; chart | superficie; exterior; manifestar; reloj | 衣 | clothes / garment | 衣 (outer clothing worn outward) | 毛 (máo, fur displayed outward) | 8 | 上下结构 | Ancient pictogram of a fur coat with the hair 毛 worn facing outward 衣 to display warmth and status, meaning 'surface/manifest'. | A fur robe worn with its fine fur facing outward (衣) displays its external surface and manifestation (表). | Un manto de pieles que luce su hermoso vello hacia afuera (衣) muestra su faz exterior y apariencia visible (表). | 214 | QMOV | 
  情 | qíng | feeling; emotion; love; passion | sentimiento; afecto; emoción; situación | 忄 | heart / mind | 忄 (heart, seat of passions) | 青 (qīng, green spring / phonetic) | 11 | 左右结构 | Phono-semantic compound: heart radical 忄 expressing human feelings, paired with 青 (spring growth / vitality). | Inner vitality and passions budding like fresh green spring shoots (青) inside the heart (忄) blossom into feelings (情). | Los brotes verdes de la primavera (青) que germinan en el corazón (忄) florecen en sentimientos y afectos vivos (情). | 35 | PQMB | 

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: When the inner feelings of the heart (情) manifest upon the outer surface of the face (表), they create a visible facial expression (表情).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Cuando los afectos del corazón (情) afloran al exterior del semblante (表), dibujan la expresión facial (表情).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: In classical Chinese poetics, 情 (innate feelings) must be externalized through 表 (manifestation / appearance). The face acts as an emotional mirror (相由心生), where subtle micro-movements of brows and eyes convey non-verbal meaning across species barriers.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Dipping 3rd tone followed by rising 2nd tone: 'biǎo qíng' (214-35). Dip low on 'biǎo', then glide upward smoothly on 'qíng'.

